WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.835
-This is a brand-new game.
I've never played this.

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:04.003
And I'm actually dreading it.

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:07.240
It's called
"Piece of Cake Trivia." Okay?

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.675
♪ -Piece of Cake Trivia ♪

00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:13.879
♪ Piece of Cake Trivia ♪

00:00:13.879 --> 00:00:15.682
-Now, our announcer,
Steve Higgins,

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:17.850
is gonna be
our quiz master tonight.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.552
Higgins, let's hear the rules.

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:20.854
-Alright, welcome to
"Piece of Cake Trivia."

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:22.789
In each round,
I'm going to ask you both

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:24.890
the same multiple-choice
question.

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:28.094
For each question, you'll
be given a tray of cupcakes

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:30.429
labeled A, B, or C.

00:00:30.429 --> 00:00:31.931
When you each have your answer,

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:34.734
you'll bite into the cupcake
you think is correct.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.969
If you're right,
your cupcake will have

00:00:36.969 --> 00:00:39.105
a delicious
creamy-filled center.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:42.942
If you're wrong, it will have
a gross mystery filling.

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:44.377
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:47.180
The player with the most correct
answers wins "Piece of Cake."

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.315
Okay, ready?
Here's the first question.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:50.416
-Okay.
-Are you ready?

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:51.884
This is called
"Piece of Cake Trivia,"

00:00:51.884 --> 00:00:53.252
even though they're cupcakes.

00:00:53.252 --> 00:00:55.688
"America's Got Talent" judge
Simon Cowell

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:58.624
has a hugely successful
record label.

00:00:58.624 --> 00:01:03.196
Which of the following acts was
never signed by Simon Cowell?

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:05.731
Is it A, One Direction?

00:01:05.731 --> 00:01:08.134
B, the Spice Girls?

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:10.470
Or C, Teletubbies?

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.206
[ Laughter ]
Hold your cupcakes.

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:16.810
-Alright, I think One Direction,
yes.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.111
Right?

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:20.379
Oh, wait, we can't help
each other, right?

00:01:20.379 --> 00:01:22.681
-I say what I think now?
-No, wait. Alright.

00:01:22.681 --> 00:01:23.950
On the count of three,
we'll say what we think

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.218
'cause I'm trying to think.
Wait, hold on.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:26.886
-And then you, A, B, or C.
You hold up the cupcakes.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:30.089
-Teletubbies are -- they're --
that's Australia.

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:31.791
Simon's U.K.

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:33.993
I'm going to say C, Teletubbies.
-Okay.

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:36.162
Sofia, do you have your answer?

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:38.298
-Oh, so I have to say something
different than he said?

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:40.199
-No, you can say the same thing.

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:42.034
-Okay, I'm gonna
say Teletubbies.

00:01:42.034 --> 00:01:43.736
-Okay, get your cupcake C.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.738
Can you see cupcake C?
Teletubbies.

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:48.074
-Can you just say "Teletubbies"
for three hours?

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:49.475
-I have it right here.
-Alright.

00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:50.776
-Okay, take a bite.

00:01:50.776 --> 00:01:52.445
-Alright, C.
Let's see if we're correct.

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:54.047
♪♪

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:55.448
-Are you gonna take a bite?

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:57.383
-Of course. That's the game.
Yes.

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:58.484
Here we go, one, two...
-Okay, take it.

00:01:58.484 --> 00:02:01.554
-One, two, three, bite.

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:03.623
Oh!

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:05.959
Delicious, garlic-filled hummus.

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:11.564
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:16.970
The correct answer was
B, the Spice Girls.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:20.139
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.139 --> 00:02:22.976
Garlic-hummus-filled cupcakes.

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:25.712
Very popular with the kids.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:28.247
-I mean, who did this?
Who decided this?

00:02:28.247 --> 00:02:30.750
-I don't know why.
I don't know why.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.685
I looked at it too,
and it looked like --

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:33.986
-Don't look at it.
Don't look at it.

00:02:33.986 --> 00:02:35.421
-Well, it is hummus. Gosh.

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:39.058
-I mean, spitting --
spitting it out is not enough.

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:41.194
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:43.662
-I agree with you.
Did you spit it out too?

00:02:43.662 --> 00:02:48.401
I couldn't even see.
-Yeah. It tastes like a salad.

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:49.835
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.835 --> 00:02:51.103
-It taste like
garlic filled hum--

00:02:51.103 --> 00:02:52.838
Alright, ready for number two?
-Blech!

00:02:52.838 --> 00:02:55.141
-I know. Sorry, Sofia.
What was the correct answer?

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:58.644
-It was the Spice Girls, B.

00:02:58.644 --> 00:03:00.480
-Oh, I thought he had
the Spice Girls.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.614
-No.
-Alright.

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:03.482
-And he signed the Teletubbies?
-Yeah.

00:03:03.482 --> 00:03:06.752
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.752 --> 00:03:08.221
-They're huge.
-He's a genius, Simon Cowell.

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:09.788
-Teletubbies were huge.

00:03:09.788 --> 00:03:11.724
-I don't want to
play this anymore.

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:15.861
-[ Laughing ] It's graduation
season for the class of 2021.

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:19.698
The student with the highest GPA
is called the valedictorian.

00:03:19.698 --> 00:03:22.201
Second highest is
called the salutatorian.

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:25.971
And the student with the third
highest GPA is called what?

00:03:25.971 --> 00:03:33.879
Is it A, historian, B,
stentorian, or C, praetorian?

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:35.781
-[ Gasps ]

00:03:35.781 --> 00:03:37.082
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.082 --> 00:03:38.550
Get your answers --
hold your cupcake --

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:40.186
hold up your cupcake
when you have an answer.

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:42.388
-Hold on, so stentorian?
-Yep.

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:45.090
Historian,
stentorian or praetorian?

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:47.059
-Okay, I think I know that one.

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:49.195
If I know that one,
you have to know that one.

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:52.232
You are American.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:56.302
-I never heard
stentorian or praetorian.

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:57.436
I never heard it.
-You see?

00:03:57.436 --> 00:03:59.839
You have to pick the one
you've never heard.

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:03.576
-Well, also, does that make
me -- Maybe I'm too dumb.

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:04.676
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.676 --> 00:04:06.045
I'm never in the running.

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:07.246
-Go for it.
-I'm gonna say --

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:09.015
-Well, you for sure
were not valedictorian.

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:10.749
-Is everybody ready?
You got your answers?

00:04:10.749 --> 00:04:12.218
-Yes.
-You got your answers?

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:13.319
-Historian.

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:14.821
-Take a bite.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:17.323
-It's stentorian.
It's stentorian.

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:19.258
-Take a bite. We'll see.

00:04:19.258 --> 00:04:25.197
♪♪

00:04:25.197 --> 00:04:27.099
It was A, historian.

00:04:27.099 --> 00:04:28.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:30.736
-Blech!

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:34.406
-Sofia, you got a cupcake
full of corned beef hash.

00:04:34.406 --> 00:04:36.008
[ Audience oohs ]

00:04:36.008 --> 00:04:39.711
An American staple for the past
200 years, corned beef hash.

00:04:39.711 --> 00:04:41.314
-Sofia, I'm so sorry.

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:43.816
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:46.719
I'm so sorry, Sofia.
I'm so sorry about this.

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:48.754
-I think we're gonna get sick,
Jimmy.

00:04:48.754 --> 00:04:50.889
Jimmy, we're gonna get sick.
-No, no, I'm sorry.

00:04:50.889 --> 00:04:53.459
I'm sorry about this.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:54.960
-Ready?
Let's move on -- question three.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:56.596
-This week Burger King entered

00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:59.131
the fast-food
chicken-sandwich wars.

00:04:59.131 --> 00:05:00.566
-Yeah.
-So sad.

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:03.369
In most countries, Burger King
is known as Burger King,

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:06.004
with the notable exception
of Australia.

00:05:06.004 --> 00:05:09.441
What is Burger King
called in Australia?

00:05:09.441 --> 00:05:16.282
Is it A, Burger Billy, B, King's
Dinner, or C, Hungry Jack's?

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:19.351
Hold up your cupcakes
when you have an answer.

00:05:19.351 --> 00:05:21.087
-What is Burger King
called in Australia?

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:22.821
-Yep.
-King's Dinner.

00:05:22.821 --> 00:05:26.259
-Go for it.
-Yeah, I say so, too.

00:05:26.259 --> 00:05:28.961
I think so.
-Ready? One --

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:31.296
Tell me when you're ready
to bite your cupcake.

00:05:31.296 --> 00:05:34.066
-Are you ready, Jimmy?

00:05:34.066 --> 00:05:36.669
Which one? I took B.

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:39.005
Okay.

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:41.807
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.807 --> 00:05:43.942
-It's tomato sauce!

00:05:43.942 --> 00:05:45.478
It's tomato sauce!
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.478 --> 00:05:49.415
The correct answer was
C, Hungry Jack's.

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:50.482
So close.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:50.482 --> 00:05:54.053
So close, Hungry Jack's.

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:56.422
Oh, my gosh.
Oh, you hear that sound?

00:05:56.422 --> 00:05:59.057
[ Air horn ]

00:05:59.057 --> 00:06:02.394
-Are you making -- You're going
to make me hate cake forever!

00:06:02.394 --> 00:06:04.330
[ Laughter ]
-Sofia, I am so sorry.

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:06.231
I did the same thing with you.
-Ready?

00:06:06.231 --> 00:06:07.566
Alright, this is
the last question.

00:06:07.566 --> 00:06:10.770
This one is worth
one billion points.

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:13.138
-A billion dollars?
-A billion points.

00:06:13.138 --> 00:06:15.107
[ Laughter ]
-Dollars.

00:06:15.107 --> 00:06:17.576
-Colombian pesos?
[ Laughter ]

00:06:17.576 --> 00:06:18.677
-Alright, here we go.
-Are you ready?

00:06:18.677 --> 00:06:19.979
Are you guys ready?

00:06:19.979 --> 00:06:23.649
Oreo just released their
Olympic-themed Team USA Oreos.

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:26.652
-Ugh, so disgusting.
-With popping candy inside.

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:29.255
-[ Exhales sharply ]
Gosh, hold on a second.

00:06:29.255 --> 00:06:30.656
What are you saying?
What? Oreos?

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:32.859
[ Laughter ]
-Which of the following

00:06:32.859 --> 00:06:36.462
has never been released
as an Oreo flavor?

00:06:36.462 --> 00:06:37.563
-Who cares? Who cares?
-And I really hope --

00:06:37.563 --> 00:06:38.764
I really hope
you get this one right.

00:06:38.764 --> 00:06:40.332
-I don't care anymore!
-I don't care either!

00:06:40.332 --> 00:06:41.700
I don't care!

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:43.369
-Was it A...
-Yes, sure.

00:06:43.369 --> 00:06:45.537
-...maple bacon Oreos?
-Yes.

00:06:45.537 --> 00:06:52.111
B, filled cupcake Oreos,
or C, hot chicken wing Oreos?

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:55.947
Which one has never been
released as a flavor?

00:06:55.947 --> 00:06:59.218
-None of them. Who would make
that kind of atrocity?

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:00.753
[ Laughter ]
-It's a trick question.

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:02.455
It's a trick question
'cause I think

00:07:02.455 --> 00:07:04.423
it's what's in our cupcakes.

00:07:04.423 --> 00:07:08.327
One's filled cupcake,
one is chicken wings,

00:07:08.327 --> 00:07:10.562
and one is maple bacon.

00:07:10.562 --> 00:07:12.165
So I think we choose.

00:07:12.165 --> 00:07:13.699
This is, like, really, like,

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:16.569
a really dark episode
of "The Tonight Show."

00:07:16.569 --> 00:07:18.170
[ Laughter ]

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:19.738
We're choosing
our own punishment.

00:07:19.738 --> 00:07:22.407
It's like a "Saw" movie.

00:07:22.407 --> 00:07:25.244
They would never, ever do
hot chicken wing Oreos.

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:27.079
-Yeah, of course, that's --
that's the one.

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:28.113
-C.
-Well, then go for C.

00:07:28.113 --> 00:07:29.315
-Let's go.

00:07:29.315 --> 00:07:30.716
-Alright, ready, everybody?

00:07:30.716 --> 00:07:32.785
-Come on, Jimmy, you can do it.

00:07:32.785 --> 00:07:35.387
Okay. We can do this
one, two, three part.

00:07:35.387 --> 00:07:37.623
-One, two, three.

00:07:37.623 --> 00:07:39.925
♪♪

00:07:39.925 --> 00:07:41.060
-It's vegemite.
-Ugh!

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:43.662
[ Laughter ]

00:07:43.662 --> 00:07:49.234
The hit Australian
dessert topping, vegemite.

00:07:49.234 --> 00:07:51.036
-Why does that even exist?

00:07:51.036 --> 00:07:54.907
I mean, a cupcake is --
it's a sacrilege.

00:07:54.907 --> 00:07:57.442
-It looked like chocolate. What?
-It was vegemite.

00:07:57.442 --> 00:07:59.178
It was vegemite.
-What is the correct answer?

00:07:59.178 --> 00:08:02.347
-The correct answer was
maple bacon Oreos.

00:08:02.347 --> 00:08:03.949
-Ugh. Who was the winner?

00:08:03.949 --> 00:08:05.885
-I think Sofia's the winner.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:05.885 --> 00:08:07.620
-I'm the winner?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:10.890
I am the winner?

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:12.758
-Thank you to Sofia Vergara.

00:08:12.758 --> 00:08:14.861
[ Cheers and applause ]
What did you win?

00:08:14.861 --> 00:08:16.929
The new season of
"America's Got Talent"

00:08:16.929 --> 00:08:19.031
premieres June 1st on NBC.

